.TH SKOGAI 1  "skogai 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai \- skogai: config, modules, and every module's commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai\fR <COMMAND>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.br
skogai: config, modules, and every module's commands
.br

.br
generated by `skogai module build` from core's templates/main.sh; rebuild,
.br
don't edit. every command runs through $BIN, so a module found after the
.br
build runs too, only without help and completion here.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
skogai\-config(1)
read and write key/value config across system, global, local and module layers
.TP
skogai\-module(1)
find, show, install and scaffold modules
.TP
skogai\-memory(1)
one fact per file, each with a stale_after; expired ones get decided on
.TP
skogai\-runner(1)
typed io for handing work to agents, prompt + files \-> json matching a schema
